# Architecture Rules

## Technology decisions

- Next.js App Router.
- TypeScript strict mode.
- Supabase PostgreSQL.
- Supabase Auth.
- Supabase Row Level Security.
- Tiptap rich-text editor.
- Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui.
- Zod for validation.
- Vitest for unit and integration tests.
- Playwright for browser-based end-to-end tests.

## Architecture

Use a modular monolith.

Organize code by application feature:
- Authentication
- Documents
- Editor
- Sharing
- File import

Keep database operations and business logic out of presentation components.

Use appropriately separated server and browser Supabase clients.

Do not expose service-role credentials to the browser.

## Data model

Profiles:
- id
- email
- full_name
- avatar_url
- created_at

Documents:
- id
- title
- content (JSONB)
- owner_id
- created_at
- updated_at

Document members:
- id
- document_id
- user_id
- role
- created_at

Use UUID primary keys and appropriate foreign keys.

Add database constraints and indexes.

Use Tiptap JSON as the canonical document representation.

## Persistence

- Save document content to PostgreSQL.
- Implement debounced autosaving.
- Track saving, saved and failed states.
- Prevent stale asynchronous writes from overwriting newer changes.
- Restore saved content when reopening a document.
- Handle empty documents and failed requests safely.

## Scope constraints

Do not implement:
- Real-time collaborative editing.
- Cursor presence.
- Comments.
- Version history.
- Complex enterprise administration.
- Unnecessary microservices.

Sharing must provide persistent access to another authenticated user.
